0378-negroni-bootargs-truncate: kern.bootargs truncates to the caller's buffer instead of ENOMEM.

Cause of the watchdogd SIGTRAP loop (docs/notes.md, section "watchdogd SIGTRAP"): 0363 raised BOOT_LINE_LENGTH to
1024. iOS 16 watchdogd (20H392, /usr/libexec/watchdogd) reads kern.bootargs once in a dispatch_once block with
sysctlbyname("kern.bootargs", buf, &len = 0x260 (608), NULL, 0). With a command line of 608 bytes or more,
sysctl_io_string(trunc 0) -> SYSCTL_OUT fails with ENOMEM, watchdogd calls _os_crash("could not retrieve device
boot-args") + brk #1 (pc 0x10000b620) = EXC_BREAKPOINT / SIGTRAP, and launchd respawns it every ~10 s.
Fix: trunc 1, so a too-small buffer gets the first oldlen-1 bytes + NUL (the 608-byte kernels gave the same 607
bytes). A size query (oldptr NULL) still returns the full length. The first 8 truncations log
"NEGRONI: kern.bootargs truncated to N of M bytes for <proc>". No watchdog hardware is touched.

--- a/bsd/kern/kern_sysctl.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_sysctl.c
@@ -2167,7 +2167,26 @@
 	char buf[BOOT_LINE_LENGTH];
 
 	strlcpy(buf, PE_boot_args(), BOOT_LINE_LENGTH);
-	error = sysctl_io_string(req, buf, BOOT_LINE_LENGTH, 0, NULL);
+	/*
+	 * negroni 0378: BOOT_LINE_LENGTH is 1024 here (0363), but iOS 16 user space sizes its
+	 * kern.bootargs buffer with the old arm64 value 608 (watchdogd: char[0x260]). A command line of
+	 * 608 bytes or more made SYSCTL_OUT fail with ENOMEM, and watchdogd hit os_crash
+	 * ("could not retrieve device boot-args", SIGTRAP) on each launchd respawn. Truncate to the
+	 * caller's buffer instead (always NUL-terminated): a 608-byte buffer gets the first 607 bytes,
+	 * which is what the 608-byte kernels returned. A size query (oldptr NULL) still gets the full length.
+	 */
+	if (req->oldptr != USER_ADDR_NULL && req->oldlen != 0 &&
+	    req->oldlen < strlen(buf) + 1) {
+		static uint32_t negroni_bootargs_trunc_logged;
+		if (negroni_bootargs_trunc_logged < 8) {
+			char name[32];
+			negroni_bootargs_trunc_logged++;
+			proc_selfname(name, sizeof(name));
+			printf("NEGRONI: kern.bootargs truncated to %lu of %lu bytes for %s\n",
+			    (unsigned long)req->oldlen - 1, (unsigned long)strlen(buf), name);
+		}
+	}
+	error = sysctl_io_string(req, buf, BOOT_LINE_LENGTH, 1, NULL);
 	return error;
 }
 
